  "html": "<section class=\"lesson-page\"> <div class=\"course-intro-card\"> <span class=\"exam-badge\"> TASK-BASED SIMULATION </span> <h2> Subsequent Events </h2> <p> Determine whether events occurring after year-end require adjustment, disclosure only, or no financial statement action. </p> </div> <div class=\"tbs-data-card\"> <h3> Reporting Timeline </h3> <div class=\"tbs-data-row\"> <span>Year-End</span> <strong>December 31</strong> </div> <div class=\"tbs-data-row\"> <span>Financial Statements Issued</span> <strong>March 15</strong> </div> </div> <div class=\"tbs-data-card\"> <h3> Evaluate Each Event </h3> <div class=\"tbs-question\"> <label for=\"tbs4-q1\"> 1. On January 20, a major customer files for bankruptcy. The customer's severe financial difficulties already existed at December 31. </label> <select id=\"tbs4-q1\" class=\"tbs-input\"> <option value=\"\"> Select treatment </option> <option value=\"Adjust\"> Adjust Financial Statements </option> <option value=\"Disclose\"> Disclosure Only </option> <option value=\"None\"> No Action </option> </select> </div> <div class=\"tbs-question\"> <label for=\"tbs4-q2\"> 2. On February 10, a fire destroys a major warehouse. The fire occurred entirely after year-end. </label> <select id=\"tbs4-q2\" class=\"tbs-input\"> <option value=\"\"> Select treatment </option> <option value=\"Adjust\"> Adjust Financial Statements </option> <option value=\"Disclose\"> Disclosure Only </option> <option value=\"None\"> No Action </option> </select> </div> <div class=\"tbs-question\"> <label for=\"tbs4-q3\"> 3. On January 5, the company settles a lawsuit. The lawsuit related to conditions that existed before December 31, and the settlement provides additional evidence about the year-end obligation. </label> <select id=\"tbs4-q3\" class=\"tbs-input\"> <option value=\"\"> Select treatment </option> <option value=\"Adjust\"> Adjust Financial Statements </option> <option value=\"Disclose\"> Disclosure Only </option> <option value=\"None\"> No Action </option> </select> </div> <div class=\"tbs-question\"> <label for=\"tbs4-q4\"> 4. On February 25, management begins preliminary discussions about a possible future expansion. No binding commitment exists and the matter is not significant to the current financial statements. </label> <select id=\"tbs4-q4\" class=\"tbs-input\"> <option value=\"\"> Select treatment </option> <option value=\"Adjust\"> Adjust Financial Statements </option> <option value=\"Disclose\"> Disclosure Only </option> <option value=\"None\"> No Action </option> </select> </div> </div> <div id=\"tbs4-result\"></div> </section>",
  "explanation": "<div class=\"tbs-results\"> <div class=\"key-points\"> <h3> Correct Answers </h3> <p> 1. Customer bankruptcy: <strong>Adjust Financial Statements</strong> </p> <p> 2. Warehouse fire after year-end: <strong>Disclosure Only</strong> </p> <p> 3. Lawsuit settlement: <strong>Adjust Financial Statements</strong> </p> <p> 4. Preliminary expansion discussions: <strong>No Action</strong> </p> </div> <div class=\"example-box\"> <h3> Key Rule </h3> <p> If the subsequent event provides additional evidence about a condition that already existed at year-end, the financial statements are generally adjusted. </p> <p> If the event relates to a new condition arising after year-end, adjustment is generally not made, although material events may require disclosure. </p> </div> </div>",
